<section id="how-it-fits" class="card" aria-labelledby="how-it-fits-heading">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h2 id="how-it-fits-heading">How the pieces fit</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <p>GatherPack was built because a <a href="https://westside-robotics.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FIRST Robotics</a> organization kept its data in scattered spreadsheets and sticky notes. Attendance, fundraising, and competition logistics lived in different heads and different files. The first fix was a small internal tool in 2014; over ten years it became that organization's daily backbone. GatherPack is the rebuild — same lessons, flexible enough for a 10-person club or a 500-person nonprofit.</p>
    <p>Members anchor everything: a person belongs to teams, teams own events and announcements, events generate attendance and finances, and communication ties it back together. You don't need all five pillars on day one — many groups start with roster + calendar and add bookkeeping when dues season arrives.</p>
    <p class="mb-0">Self-host free under the <a href="https://github.com/GatherPack/gatherpack/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MIT license</a>, or let <a href="https://sledgehammerinfosystems.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sledgehammer Infosystems</a> host it for you. <a href="/open-source/">Compare options</a> · <a href="/hosting/">See pricing</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

